# DOOM BOX — environment / credential reference
#
# This dashboard (this repo) is a static frontend only — it has no server-side
# process of its own and reads no environment variables directly. Every value
# below is actually consumed by backend fetcher scripts and Node-RED flows
# that live outside this repo, on the field-station host itself. This file
# exists so a fresh deployment knows what those backends need; wire the real
# values into each fetcher's own credential file / systemd unit, not into a
# literal `.env` this repo would load.
#
# Nothing below is required to browse the dashboard itself with mock/empty
# data — these only matter for the specific live data sources they gate.

# ── CONFLICT tab / MAP "Global Intel" layers ────────────────────────────────

# NASA FIRMS (VIIRS active-fire detection) — required for the FIRMS layer.
# Get a free account at https://firms.modaps.eosdis.gov/ . The fetcher trades
# these for a short-lived map_key on first run and caches it.
NASA_FIRMS_USERNAME=
NASA_FIRMS_PASSWORD=

# ACLED (Armed Conflict Location & Event Data) — OPTIONAL / currently unused.
# The ACLED map layer was removed from the live dashboard (acleddata.com sits
# behind Cloudflare Bot Management, which blocked the fetcher) and its
# systemd timer is disabled. These are only needed if you re-enable it.
# Free account at https://acleddata.com/register/ .
ACLED_EMAIL=
ACLED_PASSWORD=

# ── WX tab ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Not a secret, but required: api.weather.gov silently throttles requests
# without a descriptive contact User-Agent. Set this to your own
# app-name/contact string.
NWS_USER_AGENT=your-app-name/1.0 (contact@example.com)

# ── AI tab ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Ollama runs unauthenticated on localhost by design — no credential needed.
# Only relevant if you move Ollama off-box or in front of a reverse proxy.
OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434

# ── Not applicable to this dashboard ────────────────────────────────────
#
# MESH, SIGINT, ADS-B, MEDIA, SYS, MAP (regions/POI), and OSINT all read from
# local, unauthenticated sources (serial devices, local SDR, local files, or
# no-key public APIs) and need no credentials here.
